msgid "Модель и поля"
msgstr "Models and fields"

msgid "Параметры"
msgstr "Parameters"

msgid ""
"Базовый класс декларативной модели. Конструктор принимает только именованные значения объявленных"
" полей. Первый пример: :doc:`../getting-started`. Работа с файлами и буферами: :doc:`../models`."
msgstr ""
"The base class for declarative models. The constructor accepts only keyword arguments for "
"declared fields. First example: :doc:`../getting-started`. Working with files and buffers: "
":doc:`../models`."

msgid "Результат"
msgstr "Returns"

msgid "Исключение"
msgstr "Raises"

msgid "Возвращает заголовок и payload модели как ``bytes``."
msgstr "Returns the model header and payload as ``bytes``."

msgid "Читает ровно одно сообщение; байты после его конца запрещены."
msgstr "Reads exactly one message; bytes after its end are forbidden."

msgid ""
"Читает сообщение с неотрицательного offset. Возвращает экземпляр и абсолютную позицию конца "
"сообщения в переданном буфере."
msgstr ""
"Reads a message from a nonnegative offset. Returns the instance and the absolute end position of "
"the message in the supplied buffer."

msgid ""
"Возвращает отображение типов на фабрики codecs. Вызов при создании подкласса дополняет или "
"заменяет унаследованные правила. Пример: :doc:`../codecs`."
msgstr ""
"Returns a mapping from types to codec factories. Called when creating a subclass to extend or "
"replace inherited rules. Example: :doc:`../codecs`."

msgid ""
"Вызывается после присвоения полей только при определении метода в самом конкретном классе. "
"Mutation и encode повторно его не вызывают. Примеры и правила ошибок — :doc:`../validation`."
msgstr ""
"Called after fields are assigned only when the method is defined on the concrete class itself. "
"Mutation and encode do not call it again. Examples and error rules: :doc:`../validation`."

msgid "Число для элемента Constructor; не выбирает класс автоматически."
msgstr "The number for the Constructor element; does not select a class automatically."

msgid "Порядок байтов фиксированных чисел, prefixes и header."
msgstr "The byte order of fixed-width numbers, prefixes, and the header."

msgid ""
"Tuple элементов framing. По умолчанию ``(Constructor(2), Flags(8), PayloadLength(4))``. Пустой "
"tuple убирает framing. Элементы — :doc:`headers`; руководство — :doc:`../headers`."
msgstr ""
"A tuple of framing elements. Defaults to ``(Constructor(2), Flags(8), PayloadLength(4))``. An "
"empty tuple removes framing. Elements: :doc:`headers`; guide: :doc:`../headers`."

msgid ""
"Настройки задаются при объявлении класса. Служебную собранную схему не следует редактировать "
"вручную."
msgstr ""
"Settings are specified at class declaration. The internal compiled schema should not be edited "
"manually."

msgid ""
"Описывает поле; без ``index`` выбирается следующий свободный индекс. ``flag`` — номер бита "
"присутствия optional. Default и factory применяются при пропуске аргумента и взаимно исключаются."
" ``prefix_length`` и ``encoding`` настраивают автоматически выбранный codec, ``codec`` задаёт "
"готовый экземпляр явно. См. :doc:`../fields` и :doc:`../optional-defaults`."
msgstr ""
"Describes a field; without ``index``, the next available index is selected. ``flag`` is the "
"presence bit number for an optional field. The default and factory apply when the argument is "
"omitted and are mutually exclusive. ``prefix_length`` and ``encoding`` configure the "
"automatically selected codec; ``codec`` explicitly supplies a ready-to-use instance. See "
":doc:`../fields` and :doc:`../optional-defaults`."

msgid "Порядок байтов фиксированных чисел и префиксов."
msgstr "The byte order of fixed-width numbers and prefixes."

msgid "Правила объявления полей"
msgstr "Field declaration rules"

msgid ""
"Схема собирается при объявлении подкласса. Полем становится аннотированный атрибут без "
"присвоенного значения или с ``field()``. Обычное присваивание значения пропускает атрибут при "
"сборке схемы. Неаннотированные атрибуты не сериализуются. Голая аннотация ``ClassVar`` "
"автоматически не исключается; для настроек класса используйте обычное присваивание."
msgstr ""
"The schema is built when a subclass is declared. An annotated attribute becomes a field if it has"
" no assigned value or uses ``field()``. Assigning an ordinary value causes the attribute to be "
"skipped during schema construction. Unannotated attributes are not serialized. A bare "
"``ClassVar`` annotation is not automatically excluded; use ordinary assignment for class "
"settings."

msgid ""
"Индексы — уникальные неотрицательные целые числа от ``0`` до ``N - 1``, где ``N`` — число полей. "
"Если индекс не задан, выбирается наименьший ещё свободный при обходе объявления. Поздние явные "
"индексы заранее не резервируются. Поэтому смешивание способов может привести к дубликату. Обычно "
"достаточно порядка объявления; при явном задании проще указать все индексы. Индексы и имена полей"
" в байты не записываются."
msgstr ""
"Indices are unique nonnegative integers from ``0`` to ``N - 1``, where ``N`` is the field count. "
"If an index is omitted, the smallest index still available is selected while walking the "
"declaration. Explicit indices declared later are not reserved in advance, so mixing the two "
"approaches can produce a duplicate. Declaration order is usually sufficient; when setting indices"
" explicitly, it is simpler to specify all of them. Field indices and names are not written to the"
" bytes."

msgid "Defaults и создание экземпляра"
msgstr "Defaults and instance creation"

msgid ""
"Пропущенное значение определяется в порядке: ``default``, вызов ``default_factory``, ``None`` для"
" optional. Иначе возникает ``TypeError`` о пропущенном обязательном поле. Неизвестные именованные"
" аргументы также отклоняются. ``default`` и ``default_factory`` взаимно исключаются; "
"одновременное объявление вызывает ``SchemaError``."
msgstr ""
"An omitted value is resolved in this order: ``default``, a call to ``default_factory``, then "
"``None`` for optional fields. Otherwise, a ``TypeError`` is raised for the missing required "
"field. Unknown keyword arguments are also rejected. ``default`` and ``default_factory`` are "
"mutually exclusive; declaring both raises ``SchemaError``."

msgid ""
"Default проверяется при создании класса: ``None`` допустим только для optional, другое значение "
"должно соответствовать типу. Фабрика без аргументов вызывается при создании экземпляра; "
"неподходящий тип результата вызывает ``TypeError``. Списки проверяются как контейнеры, без "
"проверки каждого элемента. Диапазоны чисел и размеры значений при этой проверке не проверяются."
msgstr ""
"The default is checked at class creation: ``None`` is only allowed for optional fields; other "
"values must match the type. The factory is called without arguments at instance creation; an "
"incompatible return type raises ``TypeError``. Lists are checked as containers without checking "
"every item. This check does not validate numeric ranges or value sizes."

msgid ""
"Явно переданные аргументы присваиваются как есть, без полной runtime-валидации и преобразования "
"типов. Объект изменяем; ``encode()`` читает текущее состояние. Модели одного конкретного класса "
"сравниваются по сериализуемым полям; ``repr`` показывает имя класса и эти поля. Объекты разных "
"классов не равны, даже если поля совпадают. Автоматического преобразования в словарь нет. После "
"присвоения всех полей вызывается собственный ``__validate__`` класса; полный жизненный цикл "
"описан в :doc:`../validation`."
msgstr ""
"Explicit arguments are assigned as supplied, without full runtime validation or type conversion. "
"The object is mutable; ``encode()`` reads its current state. Models of the same concrete class "
"are compared by their serializable fields; ``repr`` shows the class name and those fields. "
"Objects of different classes are not equal even if their fields match. There is no automatic "
"conversion to a dictionary. After all fields have been assigned, the class's own ``__validate__``"
" is called; the full lifecycle is described in :doc:`../validation`."

msgid "Аннотации и наследование"
msgstr "Annotations and inheritance"

msgid ""
"Аннотации разрешаются сразу; имена используемых типов должны быть доступны. Отдельного шага для "
"разрешения ссылок на ещё не объявленные классы нет. Проще определять модели на уровне модуля, "
"вложенные классы — раньше внешних."
msgstr ""
"Annotations are resolved immediately; the names of the types used must be available. There is no "
"separate step for resolving references to classes that have not yet been declared. It is simpler "
"to define models at module scope, with nested model classes defined before the classes that "
"contain them."

msgid ""
"Подкласс со своими полями собирает схему из собственных аннотаций: сериализуемые поля родителя с "
"ними **не объединяются**. Подкласс без новых полей сохраняет унаследованные поля, но получает "
"собственную схему с текущими настройками framing. Codecs, defaults и factories этих полей "
"сохраняются; они не разрешаются заново. Самостоятельный класс без полей получает пустую схему и "
"тоже поддерживает encode/decode. Правила custom headers и multiple inheritance — "
":doc:`../inheritance`. Для композиции используйте :doc:`../collections`."
msgstr ""
"A subclass with its own fields builds its schema from its own annotations: the parent's "
"serializable fields are **not merged** with them. A subclass without new fields retains inherited"
" fields but receives its own schema with the current framing settings. The codecs, defaults, and "
"factories for those fields are retained; they are not resolved again. A standalone class without "
"fields receives an empty schema and also supports encode/decode. Custom header and multiple "
"inheritance rules: :doc:`../inheritance`. For composition, use :doc:`../collections`."

msgid "The base model class for binary serialization."
msgstr "The base model class for binary serialization."

msgid ""
"Declare fields using annotations and create an instance with keyword arguments. ``encode()`` "
"writes a message; ``decode()`` reconstructs an instance of the same class. Use ``field()`` to "
"configure individual fields."
msgstr ""
"Declare fields using annotations and create an instance with keyword arguments. ``encode()`` "
"writes a message; ``decode()`` reconstructs an instance of the same class. Use ``field()`` to "
"configure individual fields."

msgid ""
"Field values. Omitted fields receive a default, the result of a factory, or ``None`` for optional"
" fields; all other fields are required."
msgstr ""
"Field values. Omitted fields receive a default, the result of a factory, or ``None`` for optional"
" fields; all other fields are required."

msgid ""
"Annotations define the binary format, but explicitly supplied values are not fully type-checked "
"by the constructor. Fields are mutable. The schema is validated when a subclass is declared. If a"
" subclass declares its own fields, the parent's serializable fields are not merged with them."
msgstr ""
"Annotations define the binary format, but explicitly supplied values are not fully type-checked "
"by the constructor. Fields are mutable. The schema is validated when a subclass is declared. If a"
" subclass declares its own fields, the parent's serializable fields are not merged with them."

msgid "Write the current model state as a single binary message."
msgstr "Write the current model state as a single binary message."

msgid ""
"Write Constructor elements from __header__. False omits them entirely, retaining the other "
"elements."
msgstr ""
"Write Constructor elements from __header__. False omits them entirely, retaining the other "
"elements."

msgid ""
"The __header__ elements in the specified order, followed by the fields. Optional fields whose "
"value is ``None`` are not written."
msgstr ""
"The __header__ elements in the specified order, followed by the fields. Optional fields whose "
"value is ``None`` are not written."

msgid ""
"A required value is missing, or a field value cannot be written in the     selected "
"representation."
msgstr ""
"A required value is missing, or a field value cannot be written in the     selected "
"representation."

msgid ""
"Implementation errors in a custom codec are not wrapped automatically. __validate__ is not called"
" again."
msgstr ""
"Implementation errors in a custom codec are not wrapped automatically. __validate__ is not called"
" again."

msgid "Reconstruct a model from a buffer containing exactly one message."
msgstr "Reconstruct a model from a buffer containing exactly one message."

msgid "A complete binary message matching the model class."
msgstr "A complete binary message matching the model class."

msgid "A new instance of the class with the field values read from the buffer."
msgstr "A new instance of the class with the field values read from the buffer."

msgid ""
"Incomplete/invalid data, an incorrect constructor, or extra bytes after the     end of the "
"message."
msgstr ""
"Incomplete/invalid data, an incorrect constructor, or extra bytes after the     end of the "
"message."

msgid ""
"For multiple messages in a single buffer, use ``decode_from``. Unknown trailing data within the "
"declared payload is skipped."
msgstr ""
"For multiple messages in a single buffer, use ``decode_from``. Unknown trailing data within the "
"declared payload is skipped."

msgid "Read a single message from the specified position in a buffer."
msgstr "Read a single message from the specified position in a buffer."

msgid "A buffer containing the complete message."
msgstr "A buffer containing the complete message."

msgid "The nonnegative absolute position where the message starts."
msgstr "The nonnegative absolute position where the message starts."

msgid ""
"Read and validate Constructor elements. False omits them entirely; the corresponding bytes must "
"not be present in the input."
msgstr ""
"Read and validate Constructor elements. False omits them entirely; the corresponding bytes must "
"not be present in the input."

msgid ""
"A pair containing the new instance and the absolute position after the message. The position can "
"be passed to the next call to read the following message."
msgstr ""
"A pair containing the new instance and the absolute position after the message. The position can "
"be passed to the next call to read the following message."

msgid ""
"Incomplete or invalid data, an incorrect constructor, or a field extending     beyond the "
"declared payload bounds."
msgstr ""
"Incomplete or invalid data, an incorrect constructor, or a field extending     beyond the "
"declared payload bounds."

msgid "Negative offset."
msgstr "Negative offset."

msgid ""
"Trailing data within the declared payload and unknown flag bits are skipped without being "
"preserved. Bytes after the message are left to the caller. Network fragments are not accumulated "
"between calls. Without PayloadLength, the end is determined by the known fields, with no separate"
" body boundary. Creating the instance runs its own __validate__; validator exceptions propagate "
"without wrapping."
msgstr ""
"Trailing data within the declared payload and unknown flag bits are skipped without being "
"preserved. Bytes after the message are left to the caller. Network fragments are not accumulated "
"between calls. Without PayloadLength, the end is determined by the known fields, with no separate"
" body boundary. Creating the instance runs its own __validate__; validator exceptions propagate "
"without wrapping."

msgid "Define additional codec selection rules for field types."
msgstr "Define additional codec selection rules for field types."

msgid ""
"Override this classmethod in the model. Rules apply at class declaration, extending inherited "
"rules and replacing matching keys."
msgstr ""
"Override this classmethod in the model. Rules apply at class declaration, extending inherited "
"rules and replacing matching keys."

msgid ""
"A mapping from Python types to codec factories. A factory receives the annotation and "
"``FieldInfo`` and returns a ready-to-use codec instance. There are no additional rules by "
"default."
msgstr ""
"A mapping from Python types to codec factories. A factory receives the annotation and "
"``FieldInfo`` and returns a ready-to-use codec instance. There are no additional rules by "
"default."

msgid "Validate relationships between field values that have already been assigned."
msgstr "Validate relationships between field values that have already been assigned."

msgid ""
"Override this method in a concrete model and raise an exception if an invariant is violated. The "
"return value is ignored. The method is called automatically at the end of __init__, including "
"during decode, only if it is defined on the concrete class itself. To run parent validation, call"
" super().__validate__() from the child method."
msgstr ""
"Override this method in a concrete model and raise an exception if an invariant is violated. The "
"return value is ignored. The method is called automatically at the end of __init__, including "
"during decode, only if it is defined on the concrete class itself. To run parent validation, call"
" super().__validate__() from the child method."

msgid ""
"Attribute assignments and encode do not call the method again. User exceptions propagate without "
"wrapping."
msgstr ""
"Attribute assignments and encode do not call the method again. User exceptions propagate without "
"wrapping."

msgid "Configure a serializable model field."
msgstr "Configure a serializable model field."

msgid ""
"The field position, starting at zero. If omitted, the smallest available index is selected in "
"field declaration order."
msgstr ""
"The field position, starting at zero. If omitted, the smallest available index is selected in "
"field declaration order."

msgid ""
"The presence bit number (0–63). Required for ``T | None``; must be unique and fit within the "
"model's flags size."
msgstr ""
"The presence bit number (0–63). Required for ``T | None``; must be unique and fit within the "
"model's flags size."

msgid ""
"The value used when the constructor argument is omitted. Explicit ``None`` differs from having no"
" default and is only valid for optional fields."
msgstr ""
"The value used when the constructor argument is omitted. Explicit ``None`` differs from having no"
" default and is only valid for optional fields."

msgid ""
"A function with no arguments that creates a value when the field is omitted. Cannot be specified "
"together with ``default``."
msgstr ""
"A function with no arguments that creates a value when the field is omitted. Cannot be specified "
"together with ``default``."

msgid ""
"The length prefix size: 1, 2, 4, or 8 bytes, or ``VarUInt``. ``None`` keeps the codec's default "
"setting. For a list, configures the list itself, not its items."
msgstr ""
"The length prefix size: 1, 2, 4, or 8 bytes, or ``VarUInt``. ``None`` keeps the codec's default "
"setting. For a list, configures the list itself, not its items."

msgid "The encoding of text values. Defaults to UTF-8."
msgstr "The encoding of text values. Defaults to UTF-8."

msgid ""
"A ready-to-use codec instance that replaces automatic selection. Other field settings do not "
"reconfigure this instance."
msgstr ""
"A ready-to-use codec instance that replaces automatic selection. Other field settings do not "
"reconfigure this instance."

msgid "A field description for use in the body of a model class."
msgstr "A field description for use in the body of a model class."

msgid ""
"Setting compatibility is checked at model declaration. Unsupported or conflicting settings raise "
"``SchemaError``."
msgstr ""
"Setting compatibility is checked at model declaration. Unsupported or conflicting settings raise "
"``SchemaError``."

msgid "The byte order of the model's fixed-width numbers and prefixes."
msgstr "The byte order of the model's fixed-width numbers and prefixes."

msgid ""
"``BIG`` means big-endian (``>``), and ``LITTLE`` means little-endian (``<``). This setting does "
"not affect varints, bytes contents, or the UUID representation."
msgstr ""
"``BIG`` means big-endian (``>``), and ``LITTLE`` means little-endian (``<``). This setting does "
"not affect varints, bytes contents, or the UUID representation."

